// REQUIRES: long
// REQUIRES: no-sanitizer
// P04.04 (review R9): a chain of 60000 declarations is walked on stacks of its
// own (48 MB each, a new one when less than 24 MB is left). When the system gives no more stacks
// (here an address-space limit of 600 MB), the walk stops at a declaration
// with one clear error and a nonzero exit, and does not crash; the same chain
// with normal resources checks clean.
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-nesting-chain.py 60000 > %t.gopp
// RUN: not bash -c 'ulimit -v 600000; exec %gopp check -check-j=1 %t.gopp' > %t.out 2>&1
// RUN: FileCheck %s < %t.out
// RUN: %gopp check -check-j=1 %t.gopp
// CHECK: error[E0444]: nesting too deep: could not get stack for {{[0-9]+}} levels
// CHECK-NOT: error
